    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$1.22 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e, second cheapest in this entire batch. Corn and flour are the least expensive carbs in the store and they are what make up the entire topping.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eGrits are the cheap route to a corn topping.\u003c/strong\u003e They are the same ground corn as cornmeal at a lower price per pound in most stores. Check both shelf tags and buy whichever is cheaper.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCanned diced green chiles are the whole flavor.\u003c/strong\u003e They cost about a dollar a can and they bring the mild heat that makes this read as tamale pie instead of just cornbread over meat.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePork loin works here and costs less than shoulder.\u003c/strong\u003e Because it is shredded into a saucy filling rather than served in slices, the leaner cut does not hurt you.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSour cream in the batter is worth the line item.\u003c/strong\u003e It keeps the corn topping from drying out, which is the one thing that ruins a tamale pie on day three."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Season the pork loin with salt, chili powder, garlic powder, ground cumin, dried oregano, paprika and black pepper, sear it in the vegetable oil, then slow cook it until it shreds easily.",
                    "Shred the pork, drain most of the liquid, and stir in the canned diced green chiles.",
                    "Spread the pork and chile mixture across the bottom of a large greased baking dish and scatter about half the shredded cheddar over it.",
                    "Whisk the grits, flour, sugar, baking powder and salt together in a bowl.",
                    "In another bowl whisk the eggs with the heavy cream, the melted butter and the sour cream, then stir the wet into the dry just until it comes together. Do not overmix or the topping goes tough.",
                    "Pour the batter over the pork, spread it to the edges, top with the remaining cheddar, and bake at 375F for 35 to 40 minutes until the top is golden and set."
                ],
